WEBVTT

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.814
The wife poured me nice warm milk tea,

00:04:00.838 --> 00:04:02.325
and the husband offered me food

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:04.760
that they had already
prepared on the table.

00:04:05.213 --> 00:04:07.048
After some casual chitchat,

00:04:07.072 --> 00:04:09.770
the husband politely asked my purpose,

00:04:09.794 --> 00:04:11.108
so I replied bluntly

00:04:11.132 --> 00:04:12.816
that I was just traveling

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.205
and exploring my grandparents' roots

00:04:15.229 --> 00:04:17.260
and that I needed a place to stay

00:04:17.284 --> 00:04:19.332
as the sun was setting.

00:04:19.356 --> 00:04:20.604
And guess what?

00:04:21.095 --> 00:04:24.486
He said I could stay
as long as I needed to,

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.126
on one condition.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.561
He asked if I would play the morin khuur,

00:04:29.585 --> 00:04:32.372
our traditional Mongolian
horsehead fiddle.